from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
import analyze
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;d=json.loads((R/'RESULTS.json').read_text())
def esc(x):return html.escape(str(x))
def make(rows,headers):return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(x)+'</th>' for x in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>' for x in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
candidate_rows=[]
for c in d['candidates']:
 a=c['section_a'];b=c['section_b'];sens=c['sensitivity'];weak=[s for s in sens if s['status']!='same direction' or abs(s['difference_pp'] or 0)<2]
 note='Same direction in all evaluated sensitivities'
 if weak:note='; '.join(s['tr']+' '+s['arm']+': '+(s['status'] if s['difference_pp'] is None else f"{s['difference_pp']:+.2f} pp") for s in weak)
 candidate_rows.append([c['hand'],c['language'],c['position'],a+' − '+b,c['feature'],f"{c['H']['difference_pp']:+.2f}",f"{c['F']['difference_pp']:+.2f}",f"{c['H']['p_family']:.3f} / {c['F']['p_family']:.3f}",note])
exceptions=[[c['hand'],c['position'],c['section_a']+' − '+c['section_b'],c['feature'],f"{c['H']['difference_pp']:+.2f}",f"{c['F']['difference_pp']:+.2f}",c['reason']] for c in d['exceptions']]
coverage=[]
for p in d['results']:
 coverage.append([p['transcription'],p['hand'],p['language'],p['format'],p['position'],p['section_a'],p['section_b'],p['folios_a'],p['folios_b'],p['words_a'],p['words_b']])
unestimable=[[p['transcription'],p['hand'],p['format'],p['position'],p['section_a']+' / '+p['section_b'],p['folios_a'],p['folios_b'],p['words_a'],p['words_b']] for p in d['unestimable']]
body='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Section differences after controls · v49</title><style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui;color:#203739;background:#f4f2eb;margin:0}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1{font-size:33px}h2{margin-top:32px}p{max-width:1050px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #c5d1ca}th{background:#dce8e1}.scroll{overflow:auto}.note{background:#e6e6d6;padding:16px;border-left:4px solid #7c8d67}a{color:#126856}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;padding:15px}code{font-size:16px}</style><main>
<h1>Which section differences remain?</h1><p>23 October 2026 · v49 · Prefixes, suffixes and strictly internal EVA sequences</p>
<div class="note"><b>16 overlapping feature/position contrasts passed the two-reading screen.</b> They belong to a few related written families, not sixteen independent discoveries. No meanings, syllables or morphemes are identified.</div>
<h2>The clearest surviving contrasts</h2><ul><li><b>Hand 2, Currier B, paragraph interiors:</b> qo- occurs in 25.64% of bath words versus 10.40% of botanical words in H; 25.65% versus 10.83% in F. These are equal-folio mean percentages. The increase also appears at line starts.</li><li><b>Hand 1, Currier A, paragraph interiors:</b> strictly internal ke occurs in 16.04% of Recipes words versus 2.26% of botanical words in H; 15.17% versus 2.25% in F. Related keo and oke sequences overlap this same family.</li><li><b>Same hand-1 comparison:</b> -eol is 11.19% versus 1.99% in H and 10.61% versus 1.93% in F, higher in Recipes.</li><li><b>Hand 2 interiors:</b> internal od and terminal -ody are more frequent in botanical text than baths. They are overlapping spelling observations, not independent evidence for an od semantic core.</li></ul>
<h2>What was held fixed</h2><p>Exact Davis hand, Currier variety, source text format and line-position category; only loci present in both H and F. H and F were counted separately. Numbered folios combine recto/verso and foldout surfaces, and receive equal weight. The estimable comparisons were hand1/A/P botanical versus Recipes (47 versus6 folios), and hand2/B/P baths versus botanical (10 versus10 folios), each split into first/interior/last word.</p>
<p>Interior is initially a broad category. Every passing interior feature was additionally checked separately at word positions2,3,4, and every passing feature was checked among words5–8 EVA characters long. All estimable directions persisted. Several effects attenuated substantially: interior -ol and qol- fell below2 percentage points in the length-restricted subset. These sensitivities were not independently significance-tested.</p>
<p>945 features were tested in12 transcription/panel combinations. The screen uses1999 folio-label permutations, max-statistic correction across features, then Bonferroni across panels; it additionally requires the same direction and at least2 percentage points in both readings. The small permutation p-values depend on exchangeability assumptions; quires, physical layout, word families and residual topic groupings remain uncontrolled. This is exploratory conditional association, not a causal subject effect or fresh external replication.</p>
<h2>All passing contrasts</h2><p>Differences are percentage points, section A minus section B. Internal strings exclude occurrences touching either word boundary; each word contributes at most one hit per feature.</p><div class="scroll">'''+make(candidate_rows,['Hand','Variety','Position','A − B','Feature','H Δpp','F Δpp','Adjusted p H/F','Sensitivity exceptions'])+'''</div>
<h2>What did not survive cleanly</h2><p><b>-dy:</b> the controlled bath–botanical interior gap is only +4.62points in H and +3.96 in F, and fails the multiple-search screen. That is not proof of equality; it is weaker evidence than the pooled contrast suggested. <b>ot-</b> also fails this screen in the estimable comparisons. The astrology contrast itself is unavailable under the required matching.</p><p>Selected substantial direction disagreements and one-reading-only passes are listed below. Every tested feature, including nonsignificant same-direction contrasts, remains in RESULTS.json.</p><div class="scroll">'''+make(exceptions,['Hand','Position','A − B','Feature','H Δpp','F Δpp','Exception'])+'''</div>
<h2>Coverage limits</h2><p>Hand3 has only3 shared-locus botanical folios versus12 starred-paragraph folios, below the preset five-folio minimum. Most non-P formats are sparse. Astronomy/astrology has no estimable cross-section panel at matched hand/variety/format, so its previously striking qo/ot contrast cannot be attributed to section by this test. Recipes is the catalogue's section name, not a deciphered content label.</p>
<details><summary>Every estimable panel and denominator</summary><div class="scroll">'''+make(coverage,['Reading','Hand','Variety','Format','Position','A','B','A folios','B folios','A words','B words'])+'''</div></details><details><summary>All insufficient-support comparisons</summary><div class="scroll">'''+make(unestimable,['Reading','Hand','Format','Position','Sections','A folios','B folios','A words','B words'])+'''</div></details>
<h2>Interpretation</h2><p>The surviving patterns show section-linked written conventions within a hand, beyond the broad line-position mix. They may reflect vocabulary, constructions, spelling choices or local conventions. H/F agreement establishes robustness to these readings of the same manuscript, not independent replication. No ending was merged and no role classifier was applied.</p><p><a href="RESULTS.json">Every feature, exception and sensitivity</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Frozen code/input hashes</a> · <a href="../frequency-atlas-v48/report.html">Descriptive atlas</a></p></main></html>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf8')
# Scope checks independent of significance outcomes.
assert 'internal:od' in analyze.feats('qody')
assert 'internal:od' not in analyze.feats('ody')
assert 'internal:od' not in analyze.feats('qod')
assert 'prefix:qo' in analyze.feats('qody') and 'suffix:dy' in analyze.feats('qody')
for p in d['results']:
 assert min(p['folios_a'],p['folios_b'])>=5
 for f in p['features']:assert 0<=f['rate_a']<=1.000001 and 0<=f['rate_b']<=1.000001
assert all(c['H']['difference_pp']*c['F']['difference_pp']>0 for c in d['candidates'])
verification={'boundary_fixtures':'passed','rates_and_support':'passed','transcription_direction_checks':'passed','visual_inspection':'not performed; previous browser local-file policy block retained','candidates':len(d['candidates']),'features':d['features'],'panels':d['panel_tests']}
(R/'VERIFICATION.json').write_text(json.dumps(verification,indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(R/'SUMMARY.json').write_text(json.dumps({'candidates':d['candidates'],'exceptions':d['exceptions'],'coverage':coverage},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
(R/'STATUS.txt').write_text('2026-10-23: Conditional section comparison completed, H/F shared loci, hands/Currier/format/position separated. 945 features,12 estimable panels,16 overlapping two-reading candidates,14 highlighted exceptions,36 insufficient-support panels. All strict interior ordinal and length sensitivities preserve direction; some attenuate sharply. No semantic interpretation or ending collapse. See report.html.\n',encoding='utf8')
(R/'SHA256SUMS.json').write_text(json.dumps({p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in R.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name!='SHA256SUMS.json'},indent=2),encoding='utf8')
print(json.dumps(verification))
